course: dictionary
lesson: 641
title: Backward: back, reverse and slower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Backward means toward the back, or in the opposite order, from end to start. «To be on time, you plan backward from the time you have to leave.» The words plan and leave are the clues. You start at the end, the time you must leave, and work back to the start. So backward means starting at the end and going toward the beginning.
explain: Backward can also be an adjective, which describes a noun. It can mean slower to change or grow than others. Backwards, with an s, is an adverb form that means the same as backward in these uses. Both are correct, so do not worry about the extra s.
explain: Look out for phrases. «Bend over backwards» does not mean bending your body. It means trying very hard to help someone. «Know it backwards» means knowing something very well, so well you could say it in reverse. These are idioms, so you learn their meaning rather than working it out from each word.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards, such as mum, dad, Nan, level and noon.» Try reading mum from right to left: it is still mum. That is the reverse order meaning of backwards, so it fits perfectly.
fact: Backward means toward the back, or in the direction behind you.
fact: Backward means in the opposite order, from end to start.
fact: «Count backward» means count in reverse, like 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.
fact: «Bend over backwards» is an idiom meaning to try very hard to help.
fact: «Know it backwards» means to know something extremely well.
fact: A backward adjective can describe something that is slower to change or grow than others.
fact: On a number line, moving backward means moving left.
exercise: «To be on time, you plan backward from the time you have to leave.» In this sentence, backward means | *Starting at the end and working toward the start | Toward the front | Quickly, in a rush
exercise: On a number line, which direction means backward? | Down | Right | Up | *Left
exercise: «A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards, such as mum, dad, Nan, level and noon.» What does backwards mean here? | *From the last letter to the first | Toward the top of the page | Very quickly
test: «Bend over backwards» means what? | Walk slowly away | Stand on your head | Turn around in a circle | *Try very hard to help
test: Which word is an example of a palindrome from the lesson? | Chair | Table | Happy | *Level
exam: In «the little backward hook on its point», backward means | Bent into a circle | *Pointing back, the opposite way to the point | Very small | Sharp and shiny
